WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.939
Receptionist (American female): Good morning, Westbridge University Residence. How can I help?

00:04.459 --> 00:13.059
Student (British male): Hello. I'm calling to complete my accommodation application. I started the form online, but I wasn't sure about a couple of details.

00:13.479 --> 00:19.768
Receptionist (American female): Of course. We can go through it together. Before we begin, have you already received an application number?

00:20.128 --> 00:26.458
Student (British male): Yes, it's WR-4086. I wrote it down beside my passport details.

00:26.858 --> 00:30.200
Receptionist (American female): That's useful. First, can I take your family name?

00:30.500 --> 00:33.997
Student (British male): It's Chen. C, H, E, N.

00:34.357 --> 00:40.779
Receptionist (American female): Thank you. Let me just check that on the screen: Chen, C-H-E-N. And is this for the autumn intake?

00:41.199 --> 00:45.834
Student (British male): Yes, for the autumn term. I'm hoping to move in before classes start.

00:46.214 --> 00:47.835
Receptionist (American female): Right. When will you arrive?

00:48.135 --> 00:53.397
Student (British male): On the fourteenth of October. I originally wrote the twelfth, but my flight changed.

00:53.817 --> 01:00.152
Receptionist (American female): I see. The fourteenth is fine. Will you need the room for the whole academic year, or only the first term?

01:00.602 --> 01:07.046
Student (British male): The whole year, if possible. I may stay during the spring break as well, so I wanted to ask about that.

01:07.466 --> 01:13.554
Receptionist (American female): You can remain in the residence during the break, although catering hours are reduced. Do you want a shared room?

01:14.054 --> 01:18.472
Student (British male): No, a single room, please. I need somewhere quiet to study.

01:18.832 --> 01:27.043
Receptionist (American female): We have single rooms in two buildings. The older block is nearer the library, while the newer block has larger kitchens. Do you have a preference?

01:27.523 --> 01:32.028
Student (British male): The library sounds more important. I don't mind using a smaller kitchen.

01:32.418 --> 01:35.017
Receptionist (American female): That's noted. Any dietary requirement?

01:35.317 --> 01:40.195
Student (British male): Yes, vegetarian. I eat dairy products, but no meat or fish.

01:40.575 --> 01:47.224
Receptionist (American female): I'll add that to your catering profile. You can change it later through the student portal, but please give us a week's notice.

01:47.644 --> 02:07.852
Receptionist (American female): Now, several facilities are included in the weekly fee. Every room has Wi-Fi, and residents can use the bicycle storage without charge. The laundry is available, but each wash costs three pounds. Breakfast is optional, and I'm afraid there is no gym in this building. There is a small common room on each floor, and the study room has to be booked online.

02:08.472 --> 02:11.120
Student (British male): That's fine. What documents do you need?

02:11.440 --> 02:21.132
Receptionist (American female): Please send a copy of your passport by email. You can show the original at reception when you arrive. We also need your university offer letter and an emergency contact number.

02:21.632 --> 02:25.457
Student (British male): I can email those this evening. Do you need the originals as well?

02:25.787 --> 02:33.446
Receptionist (American female): A scanned copy is enough for the application. You can show the original at reception when you arrive, so please keep it in your hand luggage.

02:33.866 --> 02:40.960
Receptionist (American female): The deposit must be paid by bank transfer. We cannot accept cash for that, and the reference should include your application number.

02:41.480 --> 02:44.666
Student (British male): I understand. Is there a deadline for the transfer?

02:44.996 --> 02:52.789
Receptionist (American female): We need the deposit by the thirtieth of September. If your bank takes longer, let us know before then and we can make a note on the application.

02:53.249 --> 02:55.922
Student (British male): Right. What time can I collect my key?

02:56.252 --> 03:06.037
Receptionist (American female): Check-in begins at three p.m. You said your flight lands at two, so arriving around half past four should be comfortable. The reception desk stays open until seven on weekdays.

03:06.537 --> 03:09.430
Student (British male): Great. Is reception open late at the weekend?

03:09.810 --> 03:17.967
Receptionist (American female): On Saturdays it's open until five, and on Sundays it closes at four. If you arrive later, email us in advance and the night porter can meet you.

03:18.417 --> 03:27.196
Student (British male): Great. I chose Westbridge because it is close to the science building. The city centre residence was newer, but it was much farther from my classes.

03:27.716 --> 03:38.918
Receptionist (American female): That makes sense. Before I let you go, check that your phone number and email address are still the same as on the online form. I'll email your confirmation today, together with the move-in checklist.

03:39.468 --> 03:43.706
Student (British male): They are both correct. Thanks for taking the time to go through everything.

03:44.056 --> 03:48.611
Receptionist (American female): You're welcome. I'll email your confirmation today, and we'll see you in October.
